WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:43.760
[Music]

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:50.520
[Narrator:] Hello, here are Mary Jane and Tommy Davis.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:56.140
Let's follow them into the classroom.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.440
Shh. Miss Allen is going to speak.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:13.580
She gives out special project assignments on sleep, good posture,

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:22.300
and Mary Jane and Tommy are assigned mouth health.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:26.979
They wonder what in the world they can do with a subject on mouth health.

00:01:26.979 --> 00:01:30.729
The study of oral hygiene just doesn't seem
to suggest anything for a project.

00:01:30.729 --> 00:01:37.050
They don't realize how interesting it really
can be.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:48.920
Of course! Their friend Dr. Wilson, the family dentist, will help them.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:02:03.039
Hmm. I wonder if he's busy.

00:02:03.039 --> 00:02:06.350
Miss Young, the dental assistant, welcomes Mary Jane and Tommy.

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:11.130
They tell her about their project assignment.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:15.260
The dentist, Dr. Wilson, has just finished
cleaning Carol's teeth.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:20.140
As he has done every 4 months since she was
two years [old?].

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:24.030
Since the dentist is busy, Miss Young takes
the children into the waiting room to

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:28.970
to show them a book which may suggest some
ideas for their project.

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:32.510
[Music]

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:36.860
Each year, Carol has had an x-ray of her teeth,
which would have shown a dark spot

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:39.760
if she had had a small cavity .

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:44.290
The x-ray is a detective, which indicates
the positions of the permanent teeth,

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:49.290
which are forming here below the first or
desiduous teeth.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:54.420
This early detection helps to prevent larger
and more expensive fillings later.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:00.940
In the meantime, Miss Young has been showing the children pictures of the first,

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:04.510
or deciduous teeth, of a six-year-old child.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:08.769
The permanent teeth are forming at the ends
of the roots of the deciduous teeth

00:03:08.769 --> 00:03:12.939
noticed in the x-ray.

00:03:12.939 --> 00:03:16.299
[ Music ]

00:03:16.299 --> 00:03:21.340
Miss Young suggests that since tomorrow is
a holiday, she will take them to see the orthodontist,

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:22.590
Dr. Martin,

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.930
who has many dental models and charts.

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:29.439
And besides, Dr. Martin may even let them
ride his son's pony.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:37.980
Well, here they are at Dr. Martin's home office.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:42.440
Looks as if his son, Scotty, is getting a pony ride.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:46.060
[ Music ]

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:48.960
Miss Young will go with Scotty so that Dr.
Martin can take more time

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:51.860
from his laboratory work to show the children the exhibits.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:53.680
Let's listen in.

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:56.739
[Dr. Martin:] In this exhibit, Mary Jane and
Tommy,

00:03:56.739 --> 00:04:00.579
notice how the shape of the face changes as the jaws and teeth develop.

00:04:00.579 --> 00:04:03.810
At birth, teeth are already forming in the
jaws.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:08.930
Yet the first tooth doesn't appear in the
mouth until about six months of age.

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:14.340
Between five and a half to seven and a half years of age,

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:19.850
the first permanent, or sixth year molars make their appearance back of all the first teeth.

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:25.990
They are the most important, since they influence
the position of all the other teeth.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:32.260
At 14 years of age, the shape of the face
has taken on adult proportions.

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:37.600
All the permanent teeth are in the mouth,
with the exception of the third molars,

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:42.420
or wisdom teeth, which come in sometime after the 17th year.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:45.560
[Music]

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:52.580
Now let's go into the garden and discuss these
models of children's teeth.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:58.030
They're good examples of orthodontics, or
the straightening of teeth.

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:04.260
Now here's a picture of a boy who sucked his
thumb when he was a baby.

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:07.740
Notice how the upper teeth protrude and the
chin recedes.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:14.300
And see how his appearance has been improved by orthodontic treatment.

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:23.580
This is a plaster of paris model of a boy's
teeth before...and after correction.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:32.600
Now Tommy, you know that sleeping or resting the face on the hand may cause irregular jaws and teeth also.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:38.840
[Music]

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:42.700
[Narrator:] Now that Miss Young is back, the dentist invites his guests to the lunch

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:46.700
that has been set out in the back yard.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:58.680
[Music]

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:05.240
This properly balanced meal consists of celery--which exercises the jaws and teeth.

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:12.789
A lettuce and tomato salad and milk, the most
important of all foods.

00:06:12.789 --> 00:06:16.550
Deviled eggs. Whole grain bread and butter.

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:20.800
And fruits complete the lunch.

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:27.680
Since it is good practice to clean the teeth
following each meal,

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:33.100
Miss Young offers to demonstrate an accepted
method of tooth brushing.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:36.699
Let's hear what she says.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.900
[Miss Young:] Follow a regular toothbrushing method.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:43.270
And always begin at a definite place.

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:53.220
Put the brush high up on the gums, with the
bristles pointing with the roots of the teeth.

00:06:53.229 --> 00:06:56.610
Use considerable pressure, brushing toward
the chewing surfaces.

00:06:56.610 --> 00:07:01.449
This enables the bristles to penetrate and
clean between the teeth.

00:07:01.449 --> 00:07:04.669
Continue around the mouth and repeat on the
inside.

00:07:04.669 --> 00:07:11.009
Make eight to ten sweeps in the same location, and again on the lowers.

00:07:11.009 --> 00:07:13.990
Brush toward the chewing surfaces inside and
outside.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:20.590
Use a back and forth [method]--and be sure to scrub them well.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:36.580
[Music]

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:40.680
[Narrator:] With all that they have learned,
it is now easy as well as entertaining

00:07:40.689 --> 00:07:45.009
for Mary Jane and Tommy to make their school project.

00:07:45.009 --> 00:07:55.400
[Music]

00:07:55.409 --> 00:08:01.909
Even a neighbor's twins are inspected. What?
No teeth?

00:08:01.909 --> 00:08:19.220
[Music]

00:08:19.229 --> 00:08:30.269
With their scrapbook finished, they proudly take it to school to present it to Miss Allen.

00:08:30.269 --> 00:08:43.569
[Music]

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:46.900
The title of the book...The Value of a Smile.

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:49.580
We know how much a dollar is and how much it...

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:51.880
[Film ends abruptly; final portion missing.]

